#lang saffron
;; saffron-match-any-scrutinee-on-parametric-adt-emits-bad-c, the shape fix
;; direction 1 cannot serve: a GADT whose constructors pin a CONCRETE result
;; index.
;;
;; `(Sq int : (Shape int))` says the box holds a `(Shape int)`, and the ctor
;; widen must not touch it -- erasing an index to `any` would discard exactly
;; the type-level information a GADT exists to carry. So the `any`-scrutinee
;; narrow declines here rather than targeting `(Shape any)`, which would
;; compile and then panic `cast: any holds a different instantiation`. The
;; report is explicit that trading "does not compile" for "panics at runtime"
;; is the wrong direction.
;;
;; What is pinned is that declining is now LOUD. Before, this reached the C
;; compiler and came back as `aggregate value used where an integer was
;; expected` -- naming nothing the user wrote, and no workaround.
;;
;; The sibling `errors/saffron-gadt-skolem-escape` is the other half: an
;; UNINDEXED `defgadt` (every ctor returns `(Box a)`) pins nothing, still
;; declines, and must still reach the skolem-escape check -- so this
;; diagnostic must not swallow that one.

(defdata Shape [a]
  (Sq int : (Shape int)))

(defn area [s]
  (match s
    (Sq w) (* w w)))

(defn main [] 0)
